@startuml
title SFTP Connection State Machine (NfsSftpFsProvider / NfsSyncingByteChannel)

[*] --> Disconnected : NfsSftpFsProvider created

state Disconnected {
  [*] --> AwaitingConfig
  AwaitingConfig : no NfsSftpConfig bound yet
}

state Connected {
  [*] --> Idle
  Idle     : channel open, no pending op
  Reading  : ChannelSftp.get(path)
  Writing  : buffer dirty = true
  Flushing : NfsSftpFsIO.put() in progress

  Idle    --> Reading  : read(ByteBuffer)
  Reading --> Idle     : bytes delivered / EOF
  Idle    --> Writing  : write(ByteBuffer)
  Writing --> Idle     : buffer consumed
  Idle    --> Flushing : close() [dirty]
  Flushing --> Idle    : put complete [dirty = false]
}

state Error {
  Error : I/O or auth failure
}

Disconnected --> Connected     : open(NfsSftpConfig, path)\nNfsSftpFsIO.connect(config)
Disconnected --> Error         : AuthException / IOException

Connected    --> Disconnected  : close()\n[channel flushed if dirty]
Connected    --> Error         : I/O failure mid-operation

Error        --> Disconnected  : reconnect / user dismiss
Disconnected --> [*]           : NfsFileSystem.close()
Error        --> [*]           : fatal error / app exit

note right of Connected
  NfsSyncingByteChannel:
    position is long (overflow-safe)
    write() guards against buffer overflow
    flushes on close() when dirty
end note

note left of Disconnected
  NfsSftpConfig holds host, port, user,
  and password loaded from env var.
end note
@enduml
